---
import Frame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import { portfolio } from '../data/site';
const items = [
  {
    title: 'Why it was designed',
    body: 'To explore how a convincing product story can remain transparent about its fictional nature.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The Malaysian SME perspective',
    body: 'Clear language, useful next steps and a manageable amount of information for people running busy businesses.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Who actually built this',
    body: 'An original frontend portfolio concept by ISMAIL, the separate real website-development destination.',
    href: '/contact/',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="About" items={items}>
  <section class="container section split-section" id="concept">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">AN IMAGINED PRODUCT. A REAL PIECE OF WORK.</p>
      <h2>A concept built around a simple question.</h2>
      <p>
        What would an operations interface feel like if it made work easier to
        understand? PROWORKS explores that question through three related ideas:
        a visible process, a source-aware library and a readable report.
      </p>
      <p>
        The product company is fictional. There is no founding story, staff
        directory, customer roster or subscription service. The website exists
        to demonstrate thoughtful design and frontend engineering.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <h3>Created by ISMAIL</h3>
      <p>
        PROWORKS is an original portfolio project for the real ISMAIL
        web-development business. Follow the creator link to evaluate the work
        and discuss a real website project.
      </p>
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href={portfolio}
        data-event="portfolio_cta_click"
        data-component="about-credit"
      >
        Explore the ISMAIL portfolio ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">PRINCIPLES THAT SHAPE THE WORK</p>
      <h2>Useful before impressive.</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="lifecycle">
      <li>
        <span class="number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Begin with the visitor’s question</h3>
          <p>
            A business owner needs a clear explanation and a credible next step.
            Each page serves a different purpose, from understanding the product
            concept to inspecting the technical work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Show the consequence</h3>
          <p>
            The workflow pauses at review. The library identifies its sources.
            The dashboard exposes its figures. Every example makes the boundary
            between an illustration and a real action visible.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="number">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Keep the experience considerate</h3>
          <p>
            Readable typography, responsive layouts, native controls and
            restrained motion make the content easier to use across different
            ways of browsing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="container section reading">
    <h2>A note on the name</h2>
    <p>
      PROWORKS is the chosen identity for this fictional portfolio concept. The
      name is used by other businesses and has not been trademark-cleared. This
      project does not claim exclusive rights, legal clearance or an association
      with those businesses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Explore the <a href="/technology/">actual implementation</a>, read the{' '}
      <a href="/journal/">original field notes</a>, or{' '}
      <a href="/contact/">choose a next step</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Frame>
